  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-36348\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"36348\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"9696\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-36348\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-2\">Identifying the Type and Strength of a Given Correlation</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"36348\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <div id=\"graphic-de5e74f54ddc996a72bed66af9532323\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/de5e74f54ddc996a72bed66af9532323\"></div>\n\n<p>The scatterplot above shows the correspondence between the mean daily temperature outside a particular coffee shop and the number of customers ordering hot drinks. Which of the following best describes the correlation between the variables in the scatter plot?</p>\n\n            </div>     \n\n            <div class=\"explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n\n            <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                <div id=\"graphic-e801d5926a4792ea6ed0c746a1e43a18\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/e801d5926a4792ea6ed0c746a1e43a18\"></div>\n\n<p>We note the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The points in the scatter plot seem to follow a straight line with a <em>negative</em> slope. So, we have a <em>negative</em> correlation.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The points are scattered quite far from the corresponding trend line. So, we have a <em>weak</em> correlation.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the variables have a <em>weak negative</em> linear correlation.</p>\n\n            </div>           \n        </div>",
